			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Optimize architecture detection by using Node.js process\n\nReplace the unused browser-specific `navigator.userAgentData` logic in `DetectWebArchitecture` with a direct synchronous check for the Node.js `process.arch` property. Since Cocoon runs in a Node.js environment, this removes the need for async high-entropy value API calls and fallbacks.\n\nThe implementation now delegates immediately to `DetectArchitecture` using `process.arch`, ensuring the most efficient path for the extension host while safely returning `Unknown` if the Node context is absent.",
			"SHA": "585fed2ee1fc7687ed3be35229f8a921833a9ce7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T02:09:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1143,
				35
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Standardize DebugServer formatting and update RouteManifest\n\nReformat `Source/Debug/Server.ts` and `Source/Bootstrap/Implementation/Cocoon/Main.ts` to enforce strict 2-space indentation and linearized statement structure. This aligns the dual-layer debug server implementation with the project's PascalCase and whitespace standards, ensuring consistency across the ESBuild pipeline.\n\nRebuild all `Target/` compilation artifacts, including the new `Target/Debug/Server.js` bundle. Update `Source/Generated/RouteManifest.ts` to reflect the new generation timestamp (2026-05-19T01:54:32Z), ensuring the manifest remains synchronized with the refreshed source code and build configuration.",
			"SHA": "160ef0eaf230123a375f01b6f022187f666fa915"
		},
